  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Why DNS-01 Instead of HTTP-01",
      "items": [
        "FMS sits on a private LAN IP with ports 80/443 unavailable from the public internet",
        "Let's Encrypt validates domain control solely via the _acme-challenge TXT record in IONOS DNS",
        "Avoids FMS Admin Console's built-in HTTP-01 request, which times out and burns rate limits"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Staging & Dual-Service Reload",
      "items": [
        "/etc/letsencrypt/live is root-only (0700), so PEMs are staged to CStore/letsencrypt-staging for fmserver:fmsadmin",
        "Existing custom cert must be deleted before importing fullchain.pem, privkey.pem, and chain.pem",
        "Apache (443) reloads gracefully via httpd.graceful; DB server (5003) restarts atomically via kickstart -k com.filemaker.fms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Post-Renewal Verification (04:00)",
      "items": [
        "Runs 30 minutes after the 03:30 renewal window to catch silent deploy-hook or TTY credential failures",
        "Verifies certificate CN and expiry (< 30 days warn) independently on port 443 (Apache) and port 5003 (DB server)",
        "Tests strict OS trust store TLS via curl (no -k) and emails alerts via SMTPS without a local MTA"
      ]
    }
  ]
